(4004240, 569437, 73235, '<td valign="top">areas where I think you could improve this photo:<br/>lighting: to harsh with too many blown out areas<br/>focus: getting some area of a picture out of focus is called creative focus, everything blurry is called out-of-focus usually caused by camera shake. the use of a tripod, monopod, or something to steady the camera helps<br/>composition: a bunch of fries around a bun with an onion from a typical angle is not very inspiring or inviting to stay and explore more of your picture.</td>', 'areas where I think you could improve this photo:lighting: to harsh with too many blown out areasfocus: getting some area of a picture out of focus is called creative focus, everything blurry is called out-of-focus usually caused by camera shake. the use of a tripod, monopod, or something to steady the camera helpscomposition: a bunch of fries around a bun with an onion from a typical angle is not very inspiring or inviting to stay and explore more of your picture.', '2007-08-16 13:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
